From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:16:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(libcore): bind atl-bionic's android_getaddrinfofornet on
 glibc builds

The glibc branch of Portability.h forwarded to getaddrinfo, so a failed
lookup never reached atl-bionic's android_getaddrinfofornet, which fails
EAI_SYSTEM with EPERM when the process has no INTERNET (AOSP: SecurityException,
not UnknownHostException).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ATL glibc build; AOSP host builds keep the forwarder]
Patch-Reason: ATL is glibc with atl-bionic supplying the bionic-only API; libjavacore already NEEDs libatl_bionic, so the bionic seam is the one to call.
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 luni/src/main/native/Portability.h | 8 +-------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/luni/src/main/native/Portability.h b/luni/src/main/native/Portability.h
index 887a47b9209881d12933e3b867d49722fb277ce0..72dc7a64627a1b6b9124cfb680d6332a580e311e 100644
--- a/luni/src/main/native/Portability.h
+++ b/luni/src/main/native/Portability.h
@@ -22,14 +22,8 @@
 #include <sys/statvfs.h>
 
 #include <netdb.h>
-#if defined(__BIONIC__)
+// ATL: the glibc build binds atl-bionic's android_getaddrinfofornet (libjavacore NEEDs libatl_bionic), not a forwarder to getaddrinfo: no INTERNET answer otherwise.
 extern "C" int android_getaddrinfofornet(const char*, const char*, const struct addrinfo*, unsigned, unsigned, struct addrinfo**);
-#else
-static inline int android_getaddrinfofornet(const char* hostname, const char* servname,
-    const struct addrinfo* hints, unsigned /*netid*/, unsigned /*mark*/, struct addrinfo** res) {
-  return getaddrinfo(hostname, servname, hints, res);
-}
-#endif
 
 #if __has_include(<linux/vm_sockets.h>)
 #include <linux/vm_sockets.h>
